# The foreign project ignores what its own tooling writes, the way this project's `.gitignore` ignores `.pi/*`:
# the loop's state directory, the fixture's stub records, and the metadata pass's score list. Without it the loop's
# start-time guard reads the run's own state — created by the run itself, seconds before it reads the tree — as an
# owner's uncommitted work (issue #798, measured by this fixture's own `foreign#toolchainRunsEndToEnd`).
.pi/
nohome.gitconfig
gh.log
gh.log.bodies/
pi.log
scores.json
findings.jsonl
worker-action.sh
worker-report.txt
reviewer-report.txt
